    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, I'm Dr. Smith. It's nice to meet you. Could you tell me what brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S019",
      "patient_response": "Well, Dr. Smith, I'm here because people keep acting like I'm imagining it. It’s very frustrating. I mean, just Tuesday I was doing the floors over at the Miller house—they have this gorgeous original hardwood, the kind you absolutely can't use regular mop water on, you have to use a special oil soap or it leaves these awful cloudy streaks. Mrs. Miller is so picky about her baseboards, too, she'll run a white cloth right over them just to check my work. \n\nBut anyway, I know the hospital people and some folks from the agency have been watching our house. They think I don't notice them watching my cleaning routes, but I do. I take the 42 bus to get to my afternoon clients, and the bus driver always takes extra long at the stops. My husband used to take that same bus line years ago when he was still working at the plant. I used to pack him those little ham and cheese sandwiches he liked so much, with the mustard on the side so the bread wouldn't get soggy... \n\nBut yes, they're watching my routes to see if I'm taking proper care of my husband. I know exactly what they're up to, even if everyone else says I'm making it up.",
