    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Do you ever hear any voices or sounds that other people around you cannot hear?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S020",
      "patient_response": "Well, yes, actually. I do. Even when the house is completely quiet—and I mean completely quiet, like late at night when the neighborhood settles down. We live on a cul-de-sac, you know, so we don't get much through traffic, except for the mailman and occasionally that teenager next door with the loud muffler on his Honda. I told his mother about that muffler, it's a real nuisance when I'm trying to get my resting time in between my morning and afternoon cleaning shifts. \n\nBut anyway, when it's quiet like that, I hear this woman's voice. She's right near the kitchen window. Clear as day, like she's standing right there next to the sink. The sink is stainless steel, by the way, I polish it every Sunday with Bar Keepers Friend, it's the only thing that gets the water spots out. But she tells me to check the locks or to move my husband's pills. Just speaking right to me. I always keep his pills in that little daily organizer box, the one with the days of the week on it, but she tells me to move them. It's very clear.",
