    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Have you ever experienced periods where your mood was so low that you couldn't get out of bed, or periods where you felt so energetic and high that you didn't need to sleep?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S033",
      "patient_response": "Well, getting out of bed has never been a problem for me, really. I have to be up early for my morning clients. But there are definitely stretches where I just feel... bright, you know? Like I'm so strong and I can handle absolutely everything. I'll get through three houses in a day and still have energy to scrub my own baseboards. I use this little toothbrush for the corners—an old one, of course, I run it through the dishwasher first to sanitize it. My husband thinks I'm crazy for doing that, but you wouldn't believe the dust that gathers right where the trim meets the floor. \n\nBut during those times, when I feel so full of energy, I do notice that if my husband questions me about something, or if one of my clients tries to tell me how to do my job—like Mrs. Miller trying to tell me about dusting the ceiling fans when I've been doing it for ten years—I just snap. I snap much harder than I mean to. I don't know why, it's like a wire gets pulled too tight. My husband's sister used to get like that, actually. She lived over in Dayton and she'd call on Sundays and just yell about the most random things, like how the grocery store bagged her canned goods. I always tell the baggers at the Piggly Wiggly to put the cans in double plastic, otherwise the handles just tear right through... but yes, I do get very snappy when I'm feeling that bright and energetic.",
