    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "During those times when you feel that 'bright' energy and find yourself snapping at people, do the voices you hear happen at the same time, or do you hear them even when your mood is completely normal?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_3",
      "patient_response": "Well, they definitely happen at the same time, but... no, actually, it's not just when I'm feeling all wound up. There was this stretch recently, maybe a few weeks ago, where things were actually pretty quiet with me. I was sleeping a lot more, taking it easy, not rushing around to get all the houses done in one day. I even let my husband make his own lunch a few times, which he usually messes up—he puts the mayonnaise right on the bread and then wonders why it gets soggy by noon. I've told him a hundred times to put a piece of lettuce between the bread and the wet ingredients, it creates a barrier, you see. That's a trick I learned from this catering lady I used to clean for over in Westlake. She had this massive commercial refrigerator in her garage, took me two hours just to wipe down the stainless steel on that thing... \n\nBut anyway, even during that quieter spell when I was resting more, I still heard that woman's voice right by the kitchen window. Clear as anything. And I still knew the agency was watching us, keeping tabs on my routes. So it doesn't really matter if I'm feeling bright or if I'm just taking it easy, they're still there.",
